From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:05:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: point the P cluster's
 power gate at +0x60

The cluster power-gate node lists one PMGR word per CPU cluster, and the
bring-up switch apple_cluster_pwrgate.apply_disabled sets bit 31 of each.
The J604 node gives the P cluster's word as +0x40. The T8132 layout, as
traced from macOS on a J713 and described in the Aurora tree's
t8132.dtsi, has cluster 0 (E) at +0x0 and cluster 1 (P) at +0x60 in
/arm-io/pmgr reg[34], with iBoot setting only E's. The J604 ADT has the
same reg[34] at 0x380724000, and with both clusters up the J604 reads
+0x0 = 0x80000000 and +0x60 = 0 (apple_cluster_pwrgate.dump_sleep_words),
as that note predicts. The T8132 sleep return already writes +0x60.

The J604 boot CPU is in the P cluster. Without the P word's enable it
only clock-gates in WFI, and the sleep engine waits for every core to
power down (Aurora 3bd4bd1bf8, measured on a J700: a watchdog reset 5 s
into each sleep until the bit was set).

Point the node's second word at +0x60. The node stays disabled, so no
word is written at boot and the default behaviour is unchanged: a boot
now reports +0x60 read-only, and only apply_disabled, written for
bring-up, would set it.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index d75d1b9a9e..41890533c2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -269,9 +269,13 @@
 		reg-names = "cpu-start", "acc0", "acc1";
 		apple,pmgr = <&pmgr>;
 	};
+	/*
+	 * The CPU clusters' power-gate enables, in /arm-io/pmgr reg[34]:
+	 * cluster 0 (E) at +0x0, cluster 1 (P) at +0x60. iBoot sets E's only.
+	 */
 	cluster_pwrgate: power-gate@380724000 {
 		compatible = "apple,t8132-cluster-pwrgate", "apple,cluster-pwrgate";
-		reg = <0x03 0x80724000 0x00 0x04>, <0x03 0x80724040 0x00 0x04>;
+		reg = <0x03 0x80724000 0x00 0x04>, <0x03 0x80724060 0x00 0x04>;
 		status = "disabled";
 	};
 	pmgr_sleep: power-management@3882c8000 {
-- 
2.43.0

